# =============================================================================
# Gooey Valgrind Suppressions File
# =============================================================================
# Each entry suppresses one third-party false positive that `zig build
# test-valgrind` still reports. Keep this list minimal: an entry that no longer
# fires can hide a real bug when the code under it changes.
#
# Usage: valgrind --suppressions=valgrind.supp <program>
#
# Last audited: valgrind 3.22.0, fontconfig 2.15.0, expat 2.6 (Ubuntu 24.04).
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# Fontconfig / Expat XML Parsing
# =============================================================================
# The first FcConfigSubstitute(null, ...) call (matchFamily in
# src/text/backends/freetype/face.zig) makes fontconfig load and parse its XML
# configuration once per process. Fontconfig 2.15 leaks one 256-byte block,
# plus 64 bytes of children, inside its own expat parse callbacks. The count
# does not grow with the number of fonts loaded, and Gooey never owns that
# memory: it destroys every pattern, font set, and object set it receives.

{
   fontconfig_expat_xml_parse_definite_nested
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   obj:*libfontconfig*
   obj:*libfontconfig*
   obj:*libfontconfig*
   ...
   fun:XML_ParseBuffer
   ...
}

{
   fontconfig_expat_xml_parse_indirect_nested
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: indirect
   fun:calloc
   obj:*libfontconfig*
   obj:*libfontconfig*
   ...
   fun:XML_ParseBuffer
   ...
}

# =============================================================================
# NOTES FOR MAINTAINERS
# =============================================================================
# To check which entries still fire, run test-valgrind with `-v` and read the
# "used_suppression" lines; delete any entry that no longer appears.
#
# To add a suppression for a new false positive:
#
# 1. Generate one:
#    valgrind --gen-suppressions=all --leak-check=full \
#      ./.zig-cache/o/<hash>/test 2>&1 | grep -A 20 "insert_a_suppression"
#
# 2. Confirm from the full stack that the memory belongs to a third-party
#    library, not to Gooey.
#
# 3. Add it here with:
#    - A descriptive name
#    - A comment explaining WHY this is a false positive
#    - The minimal stack trace needed to match
#
# AVOID broad patterns like:
#    fun:*std.mem*     <- This suppresses ALL std.mem usage!
#
# Never suppress an invalid read or write (Addr*) in Gooey code; fix it.
# =============================================================================
